{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["For he could not prevail against him — the angel, and wanted to pass and flee against his will." "And he struck — it became separated from the thigh, like: ״פן תקע נפשי ממך״. [Jacob's thigh] הַיָרֵךְ — its accent is on the penultimate, at the beginning of כי תצא. And likewise: גָּדֵר מִזֶּה. And likewise: גָּזֵל. And when the resh is in construct state, they switch to become a small pataḥ and its accent is on the first letter: יֶרֶךְ יעקב. ירך המשכן."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The lemma 'בריש כי שמה' appears to be a corruption; the accentuation point being illustrated (penultimate stress in הַיָרֵךְ with qamats under the resh) matches the form at the beginning of כי תצא (Deut. 21:13), so I translate the reference as resolved to that parashah; the text as given is preserved in the translation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:08.104839204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}